    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a heavy emphasis on exploiting the favorable matchup against Kyle Gibson. **Josh Lowe** (70.08) and **Nolan Schanuel** (69.69) represent our strongest plays, as both benefit significantly from the +19% SP skill boost associated with facing Gibson, coupled with strong order placement at the top of the lineup. **Gunnar Henderson** (76.03) remains the anchor of the offense; despite a minor penalty for facing an elite base-stealing prevention strategy (Soriano), his dynamic platoon advantage and high order placement make him the must-start engine of our 5x5 production. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (68.64) is similarly positioned for success, benefiting from a high-leverage #3 spot and a favorable park factor, ensuring he remains a focal point for RBI and HR potential.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision today was leaving **Jacob Wilson** (59.19) on the pine. While he offered an intriguing +5% wind-aided boost, his status remained \"Lineup Pending\" during the optimization cycle, and his efficiency profile slightly trailed the versatility offered by **Cole Carrigg** (60.28). **Carrigg** gets the nod primarily due to his massive +14% park factor adjustment, which offsets the challenge of facing a lefty. Conversely, **Jackson Merrill** (55.00) sits near the bottom of our starting rotation due to a negative platoon split (-13%) against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, a risk we are willing to take given his steady floor. We are carefully monitoring the lineups for **Drake Baldwin**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Jackson Merrill**; should any of these players drop in the order or be held out, we will pivot to **Jacob Wilson** or **Miguel Vargas** to maximize our daily efficiency and manage our remaining game caps.",
